{
  "id": "V21",
  "title": "Strong-Wall WSWH stack and raised floor",
  "intent": "Line A: two WSWH18 panels stacked over two 9 ft stories. The 2nd-story panel uses Table 03 and is held down by the WSWH-TSS18KT kit (no tension capacity published); the 1st-story panel is checked as an allowable base moment (M_allow from Table 07, C-L-SW26 p. 50) against M_d = V₁·h₁ + V₂·(h₂ + d) at story heights (V₁ includes the upper shear; d = Setup floor plate depth), and its anchors carry the stack moment. Line B: one panel on a raised wood floor (Table 02): shear check and anchor tension T only — the anchorage is by the RDP.",
  "covers": [
    "C-L-SW26 Table 03 (stacked 2nd story)",
    "Table 07 stack base (README §5)",
    "Table 02 raised floor",
    "Table 06-A anchors",
    "TSS kit"
  ],
  "handCalc": [
    {
      "step": 1,
      "text": "Line A shears (1.0E): 2nd story F = 0.8 k → V₂ = 0.80 k on SW-1; 1st story V₁ = 0.8 + 1 = 1.80 k on SW-2. ASD: V₂ = 0.7 × 800 = 559.9999999999999 lb, V₁ = 0.7 × 1800 = 1260 lb. No gravity on the panels (P = 0 ≤ 2,000 / 4,000 lb limits)."
    },
    {
      "step": 2,
      "text": "2nd story (Table 03, WSWH18x9): V_allow = 1,095 lb → D/C = 559.9999999999999/1095 = 0.511."
    },
    {
      "step": 3,
      "text": "Stack base (Table 07, WSWH18x9, seismic): M_allow = 22585.00 lb-ft."
    },
    {
      "step": 4,
      "text": "M_d = V₁·h₁ + V₂·(h₂ + d) = 1260 × 9 + 559.9999999999999 × (9 + 1) = 16940.00 lb-ft → D/C = M_d/M_allow = 0.750 (V₁ = the story shear, which already includes V₂). Available V₁ = (M_allow − V₂·(h₂ + d))/h₁ = 1887.22 lb ≥ 1260 → OK."
    },
    {
      "step": 5,
      "text": "2nd-story hold-down = WSWH-TSS18KT: no B and no tension check — the panel's overturning is carried into the stack base moment (user 2026-11-10); the kit is OK because the panel passes Table 03 (P₂ = 0 ≤ 2,000 lb, shear D/C 0.511, drift)."
    },
    {
      "step": 6,
      "text": "Stack base anchors: M(1.0) = V₁·h₁ + V₂·(h₂ + d) = 1.80 × 9 + 0.80 × (9 + 1) = 24.200 k·ft → T = 0.7 × 24.200 / (12.5/12) = 16.262 k = 16262 lb. Table 06-A, SDC D, E rows: the pinned HS 34100 lb, W = 52 in, d_e = 18 in (STD 17,100 would now carry T)."
    },
    {
      "step": 7,
      "text": "Drift (LRFD cap with its drift): 2nd story Δ = 0.63 × 800/1565 = 0.322 in; base Δ₁ = Δ_LRFD·M(1.0)/M_allow,LRFD = 0.64 × 24200.00/32265.00 = 0.480 in (M_allow,LRFD = Table 07 LRFD-eq. 32,265 lb-ft)."
    },
    {
      "step": 8,
      "text": "Line B raised floor (Table 02, WSWH18x9, joist ≤ 12\"): V_allow = 1,475 lb; V = 1.00 k → D/C = 700/1475 = 0.475. T = 0.7·V·H_e/B = 0.7 × 1.00 × 105.25/14.0 = 5.263 k (B raised = 14.0 in) — reported; anchorage by the RDP."
    },
    {
      "step": 9,
      "text": "Line checks G1–G12 pass on both lines; the 2nd-story panel end forces are absorbed into the stack base moment (not delivered as wall-end loads)."
    },
    {
      "step": 10,
      "text": "Story drift, Line A (each story has one panel; table drift, LRFD seismic column scaled to the 1.0E share, step 7). Story drift Level 2: δxe = the largest wall δ = SW-1 0.3220 in → δx = Cd·δxe/Ie = 4 × 0.3220 / 1.0 = 1.288 in vs Δa = 0.020 × 9 × 12 = 2.160 in → OK. Story drift Level 1: δxe = the largest wall δ = SW-2 0.4800 in → δx = Cd·δxe/Ie = 4 × 0.4800 / 1.0 = 1.920 in vs Δa = 0.020 × 9 × 12 = 2.160 in → OK. The stack base carries the moment of both stories, so its Δ₁ (0.480 in) is larger than the 2nd-story panel Δ."
    },
    {
      "step": 11,
      "text": "Story drift, Line B: SW-3 Δ = 0.61 × 1000.00 / 2105 = 0.290 in (Table 02). Story drift Level 1: δxe = the largest wall δ = SW-3 0.2898 in → δx = Cd·δxe/Ie = 4 × 0.2898 / 1.0 = 1.159 in vs Δa = 0.020 × 9 × 12 = 2.160 in → OK."
    }
  ],
